-## Evidence579 — Native cache replay for a generated Lean proof
-
-The repository generator emitted identical Lean bytes after a serialized theory round trip for a fictional `True` obligation. The local Lean 4.34.1 run completed one version probe and two compilations. The bound receipt joined the selected translation digest, submitted source, and checked obligation. Reopening the on-disk cache returned the exact record, and mismatched source, profile, and obligation were rejected. Cache reuse and mismatch checks invoked zero additional Lean processes. The earlier directory identity refusal occurred before any Lean command and is retained. This evidence covers the fictional fixture and leaves statutory review pending. [Native qualification](/tmp/P1-proof-cache-translation-current-6btZZr/native-translated-cache/actual-Phase1-native-translated-proof-cache-closed.json) · [Test publication](/tmp/P1-proof-cache-translation-current-6btZZr/native-translated-cache/actual-Phase1-native-translated-cache-test-only-three-FF-publication.json)
